const PRIVACY = "## 1. Controller and scope\n\nThis Privacy Policy explains how personal data is processed when you use the mobile software application from whose App Store listing you reached this policy (the “Application”). The data controller for processing conducted in connection with the Application is Thijs Vries, an individual operating from the Netherlands (“we”, “us” or “our”).\n\nController address: Lijnbaansgracht 255, 1017 RK Amsterdam, Netherlands. Privacy contact: thijsvries1app@hotmail.com. The Application is a remote-control utility for compatible LG televisions and does not require you to create an account. There is no separate backend operated by us for Application data; however, Apple and third-party software providers may process information to deliver the services described below.\n\n## 2. Categories of data processed\n\nDepending on your use, device settings and permissions, the following categories of information may be processed:\n\n- Local television and application settings. Information about the last connected television, stored to support automatic reconnection; screen-mirroring preferences; onboarding-completion flags; and other basic local preferences. These items are stored on your device.\n- Subscription and transaction information. Subscription plan or product identifiers, purchase and renewal events, trial/entitlement status, and transaction identifiers supplied through Apple purchase services and handled by Apphud for subscription management. We do not ask for or directly store your payment-card details.\n- Device and service identifiers. Identifier for Vendor (IDFV); an Apphud-generated user/device identifier; a Singular identifier; and the Apphud identifier passed to Singular as a custom user ID. Where you authorize tracking via Apple’s App Tracking Transparency (ATT) prompt, the Identifier for Advertisers (IDFA) may be read and transmitted to Apphud. An Apple Search Ads attribution token may also be used in analytics or campaign measurement.\n- Usage and technical information. App events and analytic measurements processed through Singular and Apphud; in the ordinary operation of third-party SDKs, this may include app or OS version, device characteristics, session/event timestamps, IP address or connection-related technical information, as applicable to the SDK configuration.\n- Voice and local-network interactions. Microphone audio and recognized speech for voice search, processed by Apple’s speech-recognition frameworks; device/television discovery and remote-control commands over the local network; and device screen content intentionally mirrored to a selected television.\n- Support correspondence. If you contact us, we process the email address and any information you voluntarily include in your message to respond to the inquiry.\n\n## 3. Why we use data and legal bases\n\nWe process relevant information for the following purposes and, where the EU General Data Protection Regulation (“GDPR”) applies, on these legal bases:\n\n- Core operation and subscriptions: provide pairing, remote control, reconnection, mirroring preferences, purchase restoration and paid entitlements — performance of a contract (GDPR Article 6(1)(b)), insofar as the data is personal data.\n- Analytics and reliability: understand feature usage, measure application performance, troubleshoot issues and assess the effectiveness of distribution — legitimate interests (Article 6(1)(f)) where permitted, or consent (Article 6(1)(a)) where required by applicable privacy or electronic-communications law. Our interests are maintaining and improving the Application with proportionate measurement.\n- Advertising identifiers and tracking: access to IDFA and cross-app or cross-website tracking, if undertaken, is subject to the applicable ATT permission and any additional consent required by law; the relevant consent is the basis for processing where legally required.\n- User requests and legal compliance: answer support and privacy inquiries — legitimate interests or steps requested before or during a contractual relationship; comply with legal obligations or defend legal claims when necessary — Articles 6(1)(c) or 6(1)(f), as applicable.\n\n## 4. App permissions and how they work\n\nLocal Network: requested so the Application can find and communicate with a compatible television on the same local network. Microphone: requested when you use voice search. Speech Recognition: requested to convert spoken input into search text via Apple’s frameworks. Audio submitted to Apple’s Speech framework may be processed using Apple servers, depending on the function, device and operating-system support. We do not operate an independent voice-processing backend.\n\nApp Tracking Transparency: the Application may display Apple’s tracking permission dialog. If you decline, the Application does not obtain an available IDFA for the Apphud transfer described above. You can review or change relevant permissions in device Settings. Denying a nonessential permission may disable only its related feature; core television controls may still be available where technically possible.\n\nWhen you use screen mirroring, the content you choose to display is sent to the receiving television as part of the feature. We do not operate a remote server to host mirrored screen content. You control what appears on the television, including any personal or sensitive information shown there.\n\n## 5. Service providers and recipients\n\nTo operate the Application we use or interact with the following providers, each handling information within the scope of its relevant service:\n\n- Apple: App Store billing, subscription transactions and operating-system services including permission handling and speech recognition. Apple may process voice information and payment/transaction details under its own applicable notices and terms.\n- Apphud: subscription status, trial eligibility, entitlement management, related events and associated identifiers. The IDFA is passed to Apphud only after ATT authorization, according to the described Application integration.\n- Singular: analytics and measurement of Application usage and acquisition; it receives a Singular identifier and the Apphud user/device ID as a custom user ID, together with other measurement data applicable to the integration. Apple Search Ads attribution information may be used for measurement.\n- Television and local network: remote commands, pairing communications and mirrored content are exchanged with the television and network components you choose to use. The television manufacturer or network operator may independently process information under its own terms.\n\nWe may also disclose information to competent authorities or professional advisers if reasonably necessary and lawful, including to comply with obligations or protect legal rights. We do not operate an independent advertising network or require registration to use the Application. This policy does not state that no data is shared: the providers listed above process information as described.\n\n## 6. Signed trademark license and brand authorization\n\nThe Operator, Thijs Vries, has entered into a signed Trademark License and Brand Authorization Agreement with LG Corp. covering specified LG names, trademarks, logos and brand elements used in connection with the Application. That agreement concerns brand authorization; by itself, it does not make LG Corp. the operator of the Application, the controller of the personal data described in this Policy or a recipient of data processed by Apphud, Singular or Apple. Thijs Vries remains the data controller for processing conducted under the Operator’s responsibility. Any separate processing associated with a compatible television or third-party service is governed by the relevant provider’s terms and privacy notices.\n\n## 7. On-device storage, logs and retention\n\nThe last connected television, mirroring preferences and simple state flags (such as completion of onboarding) are retained locally until changed, reset, or removed with the Application or relevant device data. Diagnostic logging is local; we do not integrate a separate cloud crash-reporting service. This does not exclude system-level diagnostic functions provided independently by Apple.\n\nPurchase and analytics records processed by Apphud, Singular or Apple are retained under the service configuration and applicable legal, operational or recordkeeping requirements. We apply retention criteria based on the time needed to maintain subscription entitlements, generate necessary analytics, respond to requests, address disputes and satisfy legal obligations. Support messages are kept only as long as reasonably necessary for the inquiry and any required recordkeeping. Where appropriate and technically available, data is deleted or anonymized when it is no longer needed.\n\n## 8. International processing and security\n\nApple, Apphud or Singular may process or store information outside the European Economic Area, including in countries with different data-protection rules. When a transfer falls under GDPR rules, we rely on an applicable lawful transfer mechanism, such as an adequacy decision or relevant standard contractual clauses and safeguards, where required. You may contact us for further information about relevant safeguards.\n\nWe seek to use appropriate technical and organizational measures for data handled within our responsibility, including minimizing locally stored information and limiting access to support correspondence. No technology is entirely risk-free. Third-party services and your television or local network remain subject to their own technical and security conditions.\n\n## 9. Your choices and privacy rights\n\nYou can manage Local Network, Microphone, Speech Recognition and tracking permissions through the applicable device Settings. You may stop using the Application or remove locally stored application information through device controls, subject to Apple’s system behavior. Apple subscription management is available through your Apple Account settings.\n\nSubject to the conditions and exceptions in applicable law, you may request access to, rectification of, erasure of, or restriction on processing of personal data; object to processing based on legitimate interests; request portability where applicable; and withdraw consent at any time without affecting processing lawfully completed before withdrawal. Where legally required, you may also object to direct marketing and request information about relevant international transfers.\n\nTo exercise these rights, write to thijsvries1app@hotmail.com. We may ask for information reasonably necessary to verify your request without requiring you to create an Application account. We normally respond within one month under the GDPR, subject to lawful extensions or exceptions. Because certain identifiers are generated by third-party SDKs and are not linked to a named account, we may need sufficient technical details to identify the relevant records.\n\nIf you are in the EEA, you may lodge a complaint with a competent data protection authority, including the Dutch Data Protection Authority (Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens) or the authority in your country of residence or work.\n\n## 10. Children and third-party environments\n\nThe Application is a general-purpose television utility and is not designed to solicit personal information from children. If a parent or guardian believes a child’s personal data is being processed unlawfully, they may contact us to request an appropriate review. The Application is used alongside televisions and Apple services, which may have their own age requirements and privacy arrangements.\n\n## 11. Changes to this Policy\n\nWe may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes in functionality, vendors, the categories of data processed or applicable law. The current version will show the “Last updated” date. Where a change materially affects your rights or requires a new legal basis or consent, we will provide any notice or choice required by law before the relevant processing occurs.\n\n## 12. Contact\n\nData controller: Thijs Vries (Individual)\n\nPostal address: Lijnbaansgracht 255, 1017 RK Amsterdam, Netherlands\n\nEmail: thijsvries1app@hotmail.com";

const TERMS = "## 1. Acceptance and scope\n\nThese Terms of Use (the “Terms”) govern your access to and use of the mobile software application identified in the App Store listing from which you accessed these Terms (the “Application”). The Application is operated by Thijs Vries, an individual based in Amsterdam, the Netherlands (“Operator”, “we”, “us” or “our”). By downloading, accessing or using the Application, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the Application.\n\nThe Application is provided for personal, lawful use on compatible Apple devices. You must have the legal capacity to accept these Terms. If you are a minor under applicable law, use of the Application must be authorized and supervised by a parent or legal guardian where required. These Terms do not limit any rights you have under mandatory consumer protection law.\n\n## 2. What the Application does\n\nThe Application provides a software remote-control interface for compatible LG televisions connected to a local network. Depending on the television, operating system, available connection methods and granted permissions, features may include power controls, volume and channel adjustment, input selection, navigation of television applications, favorites, text entry using the device keyboard, voice search, television settings controls and screen mirroring.\n\nA compatible television, working Wi-Fi/local network and any necessary device or television permissions are required. Certain functions may not be available on every television model, firmware version or network configuration. Pairing prompts and authorization requests displayed by your television or device must be completed by you.\n\n## 3. Network access, microphone and screen mirroring\n\nThe Application may request Local Network access to discover and communicate with televisions. Voice search requires microphone and speech-recognition permissions; spoken input is processed using Apple-provided frameworks and may be processed by Apple as described in the Privacy Policy. If you deny or revoke a permission, the related feature may be unavailable, while other functions may remain usable.\n\nScreen mirroring transmits selected device screen content to a compatible television under your control. You are responsible for confirming the intended television and for avoiding the display of private, protected or third-party content without authorization. Mirroring quality depends on device capabilities, network conditions and the receiving television.\n\n## 4. Subscription plans and free trials\n\nThe Application currently offers auto-renewable subscriptions through Apple in-app purchase. Some subscription offers may include a free trial. The applicable plan, price, billing period, trial length (if any), features and local currency are displayed in the purchase flow before you confirm the transaction. Availability and eligibility for promotional or introductory offers are determined under Apple’s applicable rules.\n\nAutomatic renewal. Unless cancelled, a subscription renews automatically for successive billing periods, and Apple charges the payment method associated with your Apple Account at the then-applicable price, subject to legally required notices and consent for price changes. If you start a free trial, the paid subscription begins automatically when the trial ends unless you cancel in time; Apple determines the precise billing and eligibility terms shown at purchase.\n\nCancellation and access. Manage or cancel a subscription in your device’s Apple Account subscription settings. Deleting the Application does not cancel a subscription. Following cancellation, access to paid features generally continues until the end of the current paid period, or otherwise as shown in Apple’s subscription terms. Where supported, you can restore eligible purchases using the Application’s restore-purchases option.\n\nPayments and refunds. Apple processes App Store purchases and handles billing-related requests under its policies. Refund eligibility is determined by Apple and applicable law; statutory consumer rights remain unaffected. We use Apphud to manage subscription entitlements and related purchase information. If additional types of paid products are introduced later, their specific terms and prices will be presented before purchase and these Terms may be updated.\n\n## 5. Limited right to use the Application\n\nSubject to these Terms and payment of any applicable subscription charges, we grant you a personal, revocable, non-exclusive, non-transferable and non-sublicensable license to use the Application on Apple devices that you own or control, solely for permitted personal purposes and in accordance with Apple’s applicable usage rules. The Application is licensed, not sold. All rights not expressly granted are reserved.\n\n## 6. Intellectual property and third-party marks\n\nThe Application’s original software, interface, text, visual elements and other proprietary materials are owned by or licensed to the Operator and are protected by applicable intellectual-property laws. LG, related logos, product names and other third-party marks remain the property of their respective owners. References to LG television products identify supported or intended interoperability; they do not transfer any third-party intellectual-property rights to users.\n\nAny use of third-party brand elements within the Application is subject to the permissions applicable to those elements. These Terms do not represent that a third-party brand owner provides or guarantees the Application, nor do they give you permission to reproduce or commercially exploit any third-party marks. Technical interoperability with LG televisions does not itself confer rights in proprietary software, protocols or services owned by others.\n\n## 7. Signed trademark license and brand authorization\n\nThe Operator, Thijs Vries, has entered into a signed Trademark License and Brand Authorization Agreement with LG Corp. Under that agreement, LG Corp. has authorized the Operator to use specified LG trademarks, names, logos and brand elements in connection with the Application, including its interface, Apple App Store listing, updates and related promotion, subject to the agreed scope and conditions. The Application is independently developed and operated by Thijs Vries. This trademark authorization does not mean that LG Corp. or LG Electronics Inc. develops, publishes, operates, certifies or guarantees the Application. Ownership of the licensed marks remains with their respective owners, and users acquire no right to use those marks independently. The agreement does not itself grant access to proprietary television software, interfaces or technology beyond rights otherwise available or separately authorized.\n\n## 8. Acceptable use\n\nYou agree not to: (a) use the Application unlawfully or without authority to control a television; (b) interfere with networks, devices, access controls or security measures; (c) copy, redistribute, resell, sublicense, or exploit the Application except as legally permitted; (d) reverse engineer, decompile or attempt to obtain source code except to the extent mandatory law permits; (e) introduce malware or use automated means to disrupt the Application; or (f) violate the privacy or intellectual-property rights of others when using voice, text-input or mirroring functions.\n\n## 9. Availability, maintenance and changes\n\nWe may release updates, modify features, correct errors or discontinue functionality when reasonably necessary for security, compatibility, legal compliance or service improvement. We do not guarantee uninterrupted access, permanent compatibility with every television, or that all functions will work under all network conditions. We will provide notice where required by applicable law, especially where a material change affects paid digital services.\n\n## 10. Privacy and data processing\n\nOur Privacy Policy explains how information is processed in connection with local television discovery, voice recognition, subscriptions, analytics and device identifiers, including Apphud and Singular. It also explains your rights and choices regarding App Tracking Transparency and applicable privacy law. Please review that policy before using the Application.\n\n## 11. Third-party platforms and services\n\nApple provides the App Store, in-app payment infrastructure and system frameworks relevant to the Application. Television hardware, firmware and network services are supplied by their respective providers. Your use of those services may be subject to their own terms and privacy policies. We are not responsible for independent third-party services to the extent permitted by law, but nothing here excludes responsibility that cannot lawfully be excluded.\n\n## 12. Disclaimers and limits of liability\n\nThe Application is supplied with reasonable care and skill, subject to applicable statutory warranties and consumer remedies. To the maximum extent allowed by law, we do not warrant that third-party televisions, networks, firmware or external systems will remain compatible or error-free. Do not rely on the Application as the sole means of controlling equipment where loss of control may cause harm.\n\nWe are not liable for losses caused solely by circumstances outside our reasonable control or by your unauthorized misuse, to the extent permitted by law. Nothing in these Terms limits liability for fraud, intentional misconduct, gross negligence where such exclusion is prohibited, personal injury caused by negligence where non-excludable, or any statutory rights or remedies that cannot lawfully be waived. Any other limitation applies only to the extent valid under the law applicable to you.\n\n## 13. Suspension and termination\n\nYou may stop using the Application at any time. We may suspend or terminate access when reasonably necessary to address material breaches of these Terms, misuse, security issues or legal obligations, subject to applicable law and consumer rights. Termination does not automatically cancel an Apple-managed subscription; you must cancel it separately through Apple. Provisions intended to survive termination, including intellectual-property restrictions and lawful limitations of liability, remain effective.\n\n## 14. Governing law and consumer rights\n\nThese Terms are governed by the laws of the Netherlands, excluding conflict-of-law rules, except that mandatory consumer protection laws of your country of habitual residence continue to apply where required. Disputes may be brought before courts competent under applicable law; nothing here deprives consumers of mandatory rights to pursue a claim in their home jurisdiction where such rights apply.\n\n## 15. Changes to these Terms\n\nWe may revise these Terms to reflect product, legal or business changes. The updated text will state a new “Last updated” date and be made available through the Application or its associated listing or support resources. For material changes, we will provide any advance notice or consent required by law. Continued use after an effective change constitutes acceptance only to the extent permitted by law.\n\n## 16. Contact information\n\nOperator: Thijs Vries (Individual)\n\nAddress: Lijnbaansgracht 255, 1017 RK Amsterdam, Netherlands\n\nSupport and legal inquiries: thijsvries1app@hotmail.com";

